I was somewhat afraid of this. Looks like older iOS versions suffer from the same bug as the older macOS versions where the validation of PKCS#1 RSA padding is incorrectly rejecting empty data. The error is virtually indistinguishable from other incorrect padding errors.

I'm not sure how to proceed on this. There are two options and both may potentially result in timing attack flaws:

1) Detect the errSecParam error, fallback to decoding the RSA second time as raw data and validating the RSA padding to see if it matches empty data
2) On older iOS versions always decode the RSA as raw data and do the depadding in managed code.

I've already written and tested the second approach on macOS earlier with this depadding code:
```csharp
        internal static bool DepadPkcs1Encryption(
            ReadOnlySpan<byte> source,
            Span<byte> destination,
            out int bytesWritten)
        {
            // https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3447#section-7.2.1

            // Starts with 00 02, followed by at least 8 bytes of non-zero padding and
            // then followed by 00
            if (source.Length < 11)
                throw new CryptographicException();

            bool invalidPadding = false;

            invalidPadding |= source[0] != 0;
            invalidPadding |= source[1] != 2;

            // Count non-zero padding bytes
            int inPadding = 1;
            int paddingLength = 0;
            for (int i = 2; i < source.Length; i++)
            {
                inPadding &= (((int)source[i] + 0xff) >> 8);
                paddingLength += inPadding;
            }

            // Verify there was at least 8 padding bytes and that zero follows
            invalidPadding |= paddingLength == (paddingLength & 7);
            invalidPadding |= paddingLength == source.Length - 2;

            if (invalidPadding)
                throw new CryptographicException();

            ReadOnlySpan<byte> message = source.Slice(paddingLength + 3);

            if (message.Length <= destination.Length)
            {
                message.CopyTo(destination);
                bytesWritten = message.Length;
                return true;
            }
            else
            {
                bytesWritten = 0;
                return false;
            }
        }
```
